# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which checks text files out
# with CRLF. The files below are parsed by bash or gn on Windows runners and
# must stay LF on every checkout.
* text=auto
*.sh text eol=lf
*.gnargs text eol=lf
*.c text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf
config/angle.lock text eol=lf
